					"documentation": "One author, multiple related roots and coherent microchanges. draft is author-private; open is submitted with unresolved changes; closed has only terminal changes. Drafts have NULL submitted_at/closed_at; open has submitted_at and NULL closed_at; closed has both. Require at least one change and one source at submission, including direct staff actions. Submission freezes description, author, operation payloads, dependencies and sources; corrections use a linked new proposal. Derived partial/full outcome is not a separate stored status. Public history exposes all submitted proposals, original changes and sources, without per-change outcomes or internal reasons. All FKs ON DELETE RESTRICT.",
					"columns": [
						{
							"_type": "ERDColumn",
